<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18583" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">formīco</span></b> , āre,
			v. n.
		id.. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To creep</i> or <i>crawl like
			ants</i>: venarum inaequali aut 
			 formicante percussu, <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 51,
				52, § 171</span></i>.— * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To feel like the creeping of ants</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυρμηκιζω</span>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">donec formicet cutis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					30, 13, 41, § 120</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
